The paper is unusually short and fully constructive: its main theorem explicitly builds the cycle systems and their equitable colourings; it contains no hardness theorem or algorithmic lower bound. That rules out an honest Track A claim. I’m now testing whether the construction can support a legitimate Track B “recognize the compact coordinate change” family without making the answer either enormous or immediate from the statement.
