codex
Step 0 is decisive. The paper’s main result is not a hardness result; it is a case-by-case recipe for both the instance and its colouring. In the cyclic case, the situation is even stronger: every balanced assignment of the starter orbits to the \(s\) colours is valid, so a structure-aware candidate generator would succeed with probability 1. I’m recording this as a pre-build rejection rather than manufacturing hardness through an unrelated obfuscation.
